# JARVIS AI Starter

A small runnable starter with:
- Next.js + React + TypeScript frontend
- Python FastAPI backend
- Dark, cyan-glow chat interface
- Configurable demo response (no API key required to test)

## Requirements
- Node.js 20+
- Python 3.10+

## 1. Run the backend (Windows PowerShell)

```powershell
cd backend
py -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
pip install -r requirements.txt
uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8000
```

If PowerShell blocks activation, run `Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process Bypass` and activate again.

Backend health check: http://127.0.0.1:8000/health

## 2. Run the frontend (new terminal)

```powershell
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open http://localhost:3000

## Optional: connect an LLM
The backend currently returns a local demo response so you can run it without credentials.
To connect a provider, replace the demo logic in `backend/main.py` and keep API keys in backend environment variables. Never put secret API keys in frontend code.
